---
import Legal from "../../layouts/Legal.astro";
import { config } from "../../config";
---
<Legal title="Cookie notice" description="Which cookies olá's website uses, why, and how to accept or refuse them.">
  {config.gtmId ? (
    <>
      <p>
        This website uses <strong>strictly necessary storage</strong>, which it needs to work, and <strong>optional
        analytics and advertising cookies</strong>, which are only set if you accept them in the cookie banner. If you
        reject them, or don't choose, the site works just the same.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choice</h2>
      <p>
        When you first visit, a banner asks whether you accept optional cookies. "Accept all" and "Reject all" are equally
        easy. You can change your mind at any time:
        <button type="button" data-cookie-settings class="link">open cookie settings</button>
        (the same link is at the bottom of every page). If you withdraw consent, we stop the optional cookies and delete
        the ones this site set.
      </p>

      <h2>Strictly necessary</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>ola-consent</strong> (stored in your browser's local storage, not a cookie): remembers your cookie choice so
          we don't ask again on every page. Kept until you clear your browser data.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Optional: analytics and advertising (only with your consent)</h2>
      <p>
        We use Google Tag Manager to load Google services that help us understand how visitors use the site (for example
        Google Analytics: which pages are visited and how people find us) and to measure whether our adverts work. With
        your consent, these may set cookies such as:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>_ga, _ga_*</strong> (Google Analytics): tell visits apart and count returning visitors. Up to 2 years.</li>
        <li><strong>_gcl_*</strong> (Google Ads): link a visit to an advert you clicked, to measure the advert. Up to 90 days.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Until you accept, Google services run in "consent mode": they set no analytics or advertising cookies and receive
        only basic, cookieless signals (such as that a page was loaded, and whether consent was given), without
        identifiers that recognise you. Google processes this data as described in
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">How Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.
        Google may process data outside the UK; see our <a href="/legal/privacy/">privacy notice</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Checkout</h2>
      <p>
        When you click "Buy now" you are taken to Stripe's checkout page, which uses cookies that are strictly necessary for
        secure payment and fraud prevention. See Stripe's own cookie policy for details.
      </p>

      <h2>Your olá account</h2>
      <p>
        Your olá account (the website where you sign in) uses a strictly necessary session cookie to keep you logged in. It
        uses no analytics or advertising cookies.
      </p>
    </>
  ) : (
    <>
      <p><strong>This website uses no tracking cookies</strong>, so there is no cookie banner.</p>

      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        {config.plausibleDomain
          ? "We use Plausible Analytics, a cookieless analytics service. It counts page views in aggregate without cookies and without building personal profiles or tracking you across websites."
          : "We don't currently use analytics on this website. If we add analytics, we will update this notice."}
      </p>

      <h2>Checkout</h2>
      <p>
        When you click "Buy now" you are taken to Stripe's checkout page, which uses cookies that are strictly necessary for
        secure payment and fraud prevention. See Stripe's own cookie policy for details.
      </p>

      <h2>Your olá account</h2>
      <p>
        Your olá account (the website where you sign in) uses a strictly necessary session cookie to keep you logged in.
      </p>
    </>
  )}
</Legal>
